ignores null. If seller all null, sum null. ORDER BY DESC NULLS LAST and LIMIT 10 will include null only if fewer than 10 non-null. Could output null seller in top10, not good. Add HAVING SUM(freight_value) IS NOT NULL to rank only known. That doesn't change non-null sellers. Good. But if there are fewer than 10 sellers with freight, returns fewer, \"不足不补\". Fine.\n\nSQL:\n\nSELECT oi.seller_id,\n       ROUND(SUM(oi.freight_value), 2) AS freight_revenue\nFROM order_items oi\nGROUP BY oi.seller_id\nHAVING SUM(oi.freight_value) IS NOT NULL\nORDER BY ROUND(SUM(oi.freight_value), 2) DESC, oi.seller_id ASC\nLIMIT 10;\n\nNeed alias in ORDER BY can use freight_revenue? In PostgreSQL ORDER BY alias yes. Use freight_revenue. final.\n\nBut if ranking by final display precision, ORDER BY freight_revenue DESC. Good.\n\nNeed output only SQL. No code fence. Final must be SQL. Ensure semicolon? okay.\n\nNeed consider seller_id from order_items only. Yes.\n\nCould there be sellers with no order items? \"每个卖家的运费收入合计\" arguably include all sellers, even no sales -> 0? But question \"运费收入\" from orders, sellers with no items no revenue. If \"每个卖家\" could require sellers table left join to include zero. But taking highest 10 means sellers with zero won't be in top if there are >=10 positive. We don't need sellers table. However if fewer than 10 positive, zero sellers? Highest includes all sellers, including no revenue 0. Should we include sellers with no order_items as 0? Schema sellers. \"每个卖家的运费收入合计\" normally from order_items. To cover all sellers, left join sellers to order_items and SUM(freight_value) with COALESCE? But high top 10 likely unaffected unless <10. Rule 9: 每指标分别确定事实全集。标签覆盖会员数含无订单会员，商品均价只含已有价格；LEFT JOIN保留会员或分别聚合合并，只有明确要求有订单/商品才限缩。 For \"每个卖家的运费收入合计\", every seller including no sales? \"卖家\" entity from sellers. Since asking revenue, sellers with no revenue maybe 0. Should use sellers LEFT JOIN order_items. But if we include sellers with no items, sum null -> coalesce 0